#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# asec

#% text
# `asec(z)` gives the inverse secant.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For complex `z` the principal value is `acos(1/z)`.

#% item
# Exact special values and odd symmetry are applied; other exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
asec(2)
#% output
#= (1/3)*pi

#% cell
asec(3.0)
#% output
#= 1.2309594173407747

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
asec(0.5)
#% output
#= complex(0.0, 1.3169578969248166)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(asec(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= complex(ball(0, 3.68e-40), 1.762747174039086050465218649959585)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `atan`, `asin`, `acos`
